rds and Commissions\nTyden Center Large Conference Room Opens in new window\nTownships and Villages Opens in new window\nBarry County Opioid Settlement Funds Opens in new window\nHow Do I...\nPay a\nTraffic Ticket\nCourt Fine\nFriend of the Court Payment\nApply for\nAn Advisory Board/Commission Position Opens in new window\nA Soil Erosion Permit\nA Zoning Permit\nA Land Division Permit\nAn Inspection Application Opens in new window\nAn Open County Position\nSearch for\nBirth Death & Marriage Records Opens in new window\nFOC Court Records\nCircuit Court Records Opens in new window\nDistrict Court Records Opens in new window\nReal Estate Documents Opens in new window\nCounty Maps Opens in new window\nTax Assessment Data\nPets for Adoption\nProperty Info/Maps\nstart animation start slide 1 of 1\nSub Menu\nRegister of Deeds\nMichigan Recording Requirements\nDocument Recording\nFrequently Asked Questions\nProperty Fraud Alert\nDocument Searching and Copies\nNotary Fraud Alert\nHome\nDepartments & Officials\nOfficials\nRegister of Deeds\nRegister of Deeds\nThe Register of Deeds is the constitutional office responsible for recording, indexing, and retaining documents that convey or encumber real property in Barry County, Michigan. Recording a document with the Register of Deeds does not make it legal; it makes it public record. The office staff cannot perform title searches or provide legal advice. If you require assistance with creating or interpreting a document, we strongly suggest contacting a legal professional. For assistance with recording or searching for documents, please use the navigation on the left.\nLocation\nBarry County Courthouse\n220 W State Street\nHastings, MI 49058\nRoom 102 (1st Floor)\n__________________________\nHours\nMonday-Friday\n8:15 am - 4:45pm\nClosed 12:00pm - 1:00 pm lunch hour\n___________________________\nContact Us\n269-945-1289\nbcrod@barrycounty.org\n|\nRegister of Deeds\nEmily Reed |\nthis page\nShare this page\n×\nCopy and paste this